{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>I see him, but not now; I behold him, but not near.</b> I am a prince and the matter is far off, and it will not be near — it is a distant thing. But Moses did not say thus, but rather that the day of calamity of the nations of the world is near, and hastens for them. A parable: a king walking on the road, and with him his friend and his enemy. The king was thirsty for water. The enemy said to him: we are far from water — in order to distress him. The friend said: my lord the king, ride, for the water is near to us — in order to restore his spirit. Thus Balaam the enemy says that the salvation is far off, but the friend [Moses] says: ״שמרו משפט ועשו צדקה כי קרובה ישועתי לבא וצדקתי להגלות״." "<b>A star from Jacob.</b> The ruler of Jacob shall grow strong. דרך is an expression of strength, as in ״תדרכי נפשי עוז״." "<b>And a scepter shall arise from Israel.</b> Strong, that he shall smite the corners of Moab — of Moab. פאתי is an expression of 'she was for a corner-stone' (לראש פנה). And he prophesied concerning David, as it is said: ״ויך את מואב וימדדם בחבל״ etc." "<b>And he shall crush all the children of Seth.</b> The nations, as Rashi explained. And Israel is not included, for at the beginning of the verse he pinned dominion upon Israel."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The opening phrase 'אני שר ומעיין הדבר' is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally. The Hebrew may be partially corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:10:12.293342025Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}